harm-matrix.mjs — additive visibility patch (proposed by K65ExecHistoryC, round 65 w1)

WHY (evidence in .ufo/waves/round-65/w1/K65ExecHistoryC.md findings -1 and -2, and
build/K65ExecHistoryC/direct-runs.txt):

  * A gate that emits no verdict line at EITHER revision becomes a CARRIED row, is
    counted in `gates=`, and is invisible in the summary. The matrix then prints
    `HARM_MATRIX: CLEAN` and exits 0 while one of the "measured" gates produced nothing.
    Real revisions: node scripts/harm-matrix.mjs --lane . \
      --base f86b8ed0 --tip 364f1d59 --only surface-known --timeout 120
      -> HARM_MATRIX: CLEAN gates=1 held=0 repaired=0 carried=1 ... exit 0
         (the single row is base=FAIL_CLOSED tip=FAIL_CLOSED "no-verdict exit=64")
    Full pair A (f86b8ed0 -> 364f1d59) reads `CLEAN gates=5` with 1 of the 5 blind.
  * Pair B (0ecba269 -> 89ff4a74) exits 1 on NEW_RED minted from a tip that did not
    run (`TRUTH: FAIL-CLOSED (SRC_MISSING ...)` exit 2), i.e. from an unreadable gate.

WHAT IT CHANGES: one new output line. No class change, no exit-code change, no
relaxation. `HARM_MATRIX_UNREADABLE:` does not share the `HARM_MATRIX: ` prefix, so the
frozen harness (rows from `HARM_ROW `, summary from `HARM_MATRIX: `) is unaffected.
The line is printed after the rows and before the summary.

--- a/scripts/harm-matrix.mjs
+++ b/scripts/harm-matrix.mjs
@@ -142,6 +142,8 @@
   for (const r of res.rows) out(`HARM_ROW gate=${r.gate} base=${r.b.cls} tip=${r.t.cls} id=${r.id} base_text=${JSON.stringify(r.b.text)} tip_text=${JSON.stringify(r.t.text)}`);
   const counted = res.rows.filter((r) => r.id !== 'ABSENT_BOTH').length;
   if (counted === 0) failClosed('NO_GATES', 'every gate absent at both revisions');
+  const unreadable = res.rows.filter((r) => r.id !== 'ABSENT_BOTH' && [r.b.cls, r.t.cls].some((c) => c === 'FAIL_CLOSED' || c === 'TIMEOUT'));
+  if (unreadable.length) out(`HARM_MATRIX_UNREADABLE: count=${unreadable.length} gates=${unreadable.map((r) => `${r.gate}:${r.b.cls}/${r.t.cls}`).join(',')}`);
   const harm = n('HARM'), harmAbsent = n('HARM_ABSENT'), newRed = n('NEW_RED');
   const bad = harm + harmAbsent + newRed;
   out(`HARM_MATRIX: ${bad === 0 ? 'CLEAN' : 'HARM'} gates=${counted} held=${n('HELD')} repaired=${n('REPAIRED')} carried=${n('CARRIED')} moved=${n('CARRIED_MOVED')} new=${n('NEW_OK')} gone=${n('GONE')} harm=${harm} harm_absent=${harmAbsent} new_red=${newRed} base=${res.revs.base.slice(0, 12)} tip=${res.revs.tip.slice(0, 12)}`);

